  "id": "DrugBank_DB06185 - MONDO_15812",
  "verbalization": "Forodesine is associated with Primary Cutaneous Gamma/delta-positive T-cell Lymphoma through a chain of indications involving Pralatrexate. The evidence suggests that Forodesine is linked to Peripheral T-cell Lymphoma, Not Otherwise Specified, which in turn is linked to Pralatrexate, and Pralatrexate is linked to Primary Cutaneous Gamma/delta-positive T-cell Lymphoma. This implies a potential pathway where Forodesine may influence the development or progression of this lymphoma through its interaction with Pralatrexate. The shared use of Pralatrexate in multiple pathways supports the idea that Forodesine could be part of a broader therapeutic context for this condition. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, suggesting a possible mechanistic link that involves the use of Pralatrexate as a mediator in the relationship between Forodesine and the lymphoma.",
